  "name": "Residual Plots",
  "problem": "A **residual plot** displays the values of the independent variable along the horizontal axis and the residuals along the vertical axis. \n\nThe scatter plot below represents data from a four-day sample on the number of people visiting a swimming pool and the average daytime temperature, in degrees Celsius. The line $\\ell$ is the corresponding linear regression line. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14233881/assets/6228578012fac7e42bedeb7ab7ad5fc9f42432aed8d5751b675df560bc867417.png)\n\n    \n\nThese residuals for each of the four data points are highlighted below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14233881/assets/d70c44fe7b8fce43a8962ac104651acced75e10598e865a3b3c80d09f16ce234.png)\n\n    \n\nIf we calculate the numerical values for the residuals at each data point (from left to right), we get the following results:\n\n$$\n-4, \\quad 8, \\quad -8, \\quad 4\n$$\n\nTo compute our residual plot, we plot each $x$-value and its corresponding residual on some coordinate axes: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14233881/assets/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)",
